%% M6 public tracking page: a guest with only a tracking number sees a masked, live timeline.
%% The REST call is public (no token); the socket joins the public room tracking:<no> only.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor GU as Guest (no login)
    participant WEB as Next.js public page<br/>/track/[trackingNumber]
    participant GW as api-gateway<br/>rate limit by client IP
    participant TS as tracking-service<br/>TrackingQueryService
    participant DB as MongoDB
    participant SG as Socket.IO gateway<br/>/ws/tracking

    GU->>WEB: open /track/TRACKING_NO on a phone
    WEB->>GW: GET /api/v1/tracking/public/{trackingNumber}
    GW->>GW: enumeration guard: count lookups per IP
    alt lookups over the limit
        GW-->>WEB: 429 problem+json, Retry-After
    else within the limit
        GW->>TS: forward, no bearer token needed
        TS->>DB: find by trackingNumber, projection = publicView only
        alt tracking number unknown
            TS-->>GW: 404 problem+json
        else found
            DB-->>TS: publicView (status, city, masked recipient, steps)
            TS-->>GW: 200 PublicTrackingView, no phone, no street
            GW-->>WEB: 200
        end
    end
    WEB-->>GU: stepper, last update time, city-level location

    WEB->>SG: connect /ws/tracking (no auth.token)
    SG-->>WEB: connected
    WEB->>SG: join tracking:TRACKING_NO
    SG->>SG: RoomPolicy: tracking: rooms are public
    SG-->>WEB: joined
    Note over SG,WEB: later, a status change arrives
    SG-->>WEB: parcel.status (same payload as the REST view)
    WEB-->>GU: stepper advances, no refresh needed
